    "Response": "I think in modern day society we've gotten past rigid and strict gender roles and now we're in the stage of equality where women do anything men can do, rather than being tied down to specific jobs or roles as housewives or homemakers. Men and women are viewed as people first before gender nowadays which is an important shift. From a religious stance, I think that everyone is equal in the eyes of God, but I think that women and men have different roles and purposes in their families. Men are the head of the family, and women are more like the \"coverings for the men\" like God grafted Adam to Eve in the first place. 
    In the church, I think that women and men are both equal. Men aren't better than women and women aren't better than men. Instead both men and women have different roles in church and in the body of Christ. Men are the teachers of the Word and are the leaders of the family and the church and they pastor. Women support the men and fulfill a submissive role. Women can be helpers in church as teachers but not at the level a the man in ministering the Word. 
    So, in summary I think that historically women and men's roles have been very fixed and restricted, similar to the idea of Father knows best or what have you. I think women and men can now do the same things such as women working outside the home as a career regardless of component and still maintaining their families. But on a religious level, gender roles and the roles of women and men are different but the same; they're equally important and both are crucial in the function of the home and of the church. "
