idea_1 = If you don't want to get divorce, but you are finding it difficult to argue and you don't want to get in domestic violence with your spouse (or if your spouse is abusive, only in this case, you should definitely consider divorce), then what I would recommend doing is:

1.) Have a conversation with your partner and let them know how you feel. This will create a plan of action to make things better;

2.) Suggest counseling (because they are not there to place blame, but unify the marriage in a more positive manner);

3.) Take a step back and reflect on your marriage and the bigger parts of your relationship (like the things that you didn't look at before you got married - like education, desire, etc). Then make a decision on whether you would like pursuing it further (or considering even separation).

Hope this helps. Good luck.
